===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*megʰ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|maught}}, {{m|enm|might}}, {{m|enm|miȝt}}, {{m|enm|myght}}, from {{inh|en|ang|maht}}, {{m|ang|meaht}}, {{m|ang|meht}}, {{m|ang|mieht}}, {{m|ang|miht}}, {{m|ang|mæht|t=ability, power; strength; virtue}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*mahti}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*mahtiz|t=ability, power; force, strength}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*(me)mógʰe|t=to be able to, to have power}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*megʰ-|t=to be able}}, corresponding to Germanic {{m|gem-pro|*maganą|t=to be able, may}} + {{m|gem-pro|*-þiz}}. Equivalent to {{m|en|may}} {{suf|en||-th|nocat=1}}.
{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|sco|micht|t=might}}, {{cog|yol|mought|t=might}}, {{cog|nl|macht|t=might, power}}, {{cog|de|Macht|t=might, power}}, {{cog|lb|Muecht|t=authority, might, power}}, {{cog|yi|מאַכט|t=might, power}}, {{cog|fo,is|máttur|t=might, strength}}, {{cog|da|magt|t=power; force}}, {{cog|nb|makt|t=power}}, {{cog|nn,sv|makt|t=power; force}}, {{m|sv|mått|t=might, power}}, {{cog|got|𐌼𐌰𐌷𐍄𐍃|t=ability, might, power}}, and further to {{cog|ga|smacht|t=ordinance, regulation, rule; dominion, sway; control, discipline, restraint; fine, penalty}}, {{cog|el|μάγος|t=magician; sorcerer, wizard}}, {{cog|lt|mėgti|t=to like}}, {{cog|be|моц|t=might, power}}, {{cog|bg|мощ|t=might, power}}, {{cog|cs,pl|moc|t=might, power}}, {{cog|mk|моќ|t=might, power}}, {{cog|ru|мочь|t=power, might}} and {{m|ru|мощь|t=force, strength}}, {{cog|sh|мо̑ћ}}, {{m|sh|mȏć|t=power; strength; potency; authority}}, {{cog|sl|moč|t=power; strength}}, {{cog|uk|міч}} and {{m|uk|міць|t=might, power}}, {{cog|hy|մոգ|t=magus; fire-worshiper, Zoroastrian; astrologer; diviner, enchanter, sorcerer, wizard}}, {{cog|fa|مغ|tr=moġ|t=magus}}, {{cog|sa|मघ|t=power, wealth; bounty, gift, reward}}. See more at {{l|en|may}}.
